# Context

Part of T066: bound every execution path that evaluates untrusted
patterns. Pack and contract-variant artifacts reach a first-party
process from disk, so their schemas and instances are untrusted even
though the schemas themselves ship with the repository. The hostile
case is a fixed schema plus an adversarial instance: catastrophic
backtracking needs only one hostile operand.

Follows the pattern set by 0e92cd5/9e499bf: the schema set exposes
raw documents only, and validateSchemaInstance compiles and executes
in the schema worker. The in-process SchemaValidator cache is gone on
purpose — keeping it would leave a second, unbounded compile path.

Gotcha: grep treats packages/pack/src/manifest.ts as binary (raw NUL
in a template literal at line 517); use grep -a on that file.
